// deep without the Podman sandbox, with an explicit tool list (2026-11-22, Adam: "fix it so that it
// works with the deep" on the Max plan). On the Max lane deep runs on claude-cli, which OpenClaw
// refuses for a sandboxed child: "This spawn targets a sandboxed child, but model
// anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 runs on host-executed CLI backend claude-cli and cannot honor the
// sandbox" (main's Claude Code transcript, 14:58:55 UTC). So deep's own sandbox is off on both lanes.
//
// Why this is safe: deep needs no shell or files. A managed claude-cli turn gets none of Claude's
// native tools, only OpenClaw's, through the grant-scoped MCP server and under OpenClaw's policy
// (OpenClaw docs gateway/cli-backends.md). Without the sandbox its sandbox tool list no longer
// applies, so tools.allow names the only tools deep keeps: the web, the read-only browser, the
// price sums and tool search. The deny list stays as it was. jorah-guard enforces the same list
// (permission-matrix consultTools), so a drift here still can't reach read, memory or the supplies
// record. The browser is Jorah's own host profile, as main's is; the guard keeps it to reading.
//
// Apply after the guard with consultTools is live. Undo: config unset agents.entries.deep.sandbox
// and agents.entries.deep.tools.allow (deep goes back to the default sandbox, and on the Max lane
// spawns fail again).
{
  agents: {
    entries: {
      deep: {
        sandbox: { mode: "off" },
        tools: { allow: ["web_search", "x_search", "web_fetch", "browser", "price_compare", "tool_search", "tool_describe"] },
      },
    },
  },
}
